// =============================================================================
// Enterprise License Management System (ELMS) - team VFast
// Database design (DBML) - design status: TARGET, nothing implemented yet
//
// Sources: README.md, docs/01-research-top-down.md, docs/02-use-cases.md
//          (third revision, 2026-11-15), docs/08-feature-list.md.
// UCxx / BR-xx / Ax in the notes refer to those documents. Dxx refers to the
// decisions below; docs/database/README.md explains each one.
//
// Render: paste into https://dbdiagram.io or run `npx -p @dbml/cli dbml2sql
//         docs/database/elms.dbml --postgres` (validated with @dbml/cli 12.0.0).
//         Reference DDL: docs/database/schema.sql. ERD per group:
//         docs/database/diagrams/ (python docs/diagrams/ve_erd.py).
//
// Business model (docs/02, P&L API model). ELMS reads licenses, holders, and
// usage from one usage connector per company and provider, employees and units
// from ILVG, application usage from BCA, and the budget plan from an Excel
// import. Nobody enters a license in ELMS (BR-01).
//
// Decisions kept from the first design:
//   D1.  A "license" is a license plan (one tier or SKU, e.g. Microsoft 365 E3)
//        reported by one connector for one company. Holders, usage, budget
//        lines, and expenses point to the plan; an entitlement line is one
//        purchase or term of that plan as the connector reports it.
//   D2.  Employees (directory) and user accounts (login) are separate tables.
//   D5.  Two cost views: billed = expenses (invoices); effective = the monthly
//        cost split to units in cost_allocations. Since D33 the effective cost
//        of a month is the accrual of the expenses.
//   D7.  Per-seat status needs per-subject usage; an aggregate-only source
//        leaves seats Not monitored.
//   D8.  Completeness per plan, kind of data, and day (collection_coverage).
//   D9.  History is kept by freezing results: daily snapshots, and
//        cost_allocations frozen when a month closes.
//   D10. Every plan has an owner unit (see D27).
//   D12. One reporting currency (VND); amounts converted with the rate of the
//        day, then frozen.
//   D13. Metered overuse = consumption over the validity of a line with a quota.
//   D14. Months close on a set day of the next month unless Staff close them
//        first (UC42); leavers' accounts are disabled automatically.
//   D20. Leavers: employees.left_on; the leaver check also reads
//        subjects.is_enabled.
//   D22. A new account gets a one-time link to set its first password.
//
// Decisions superseded by the business model:
//   D3, D19 (quotas per unit), D4 (one yearly budget per unit), D6 (service
//   month), D11 (one tenant per vendor), D15, D16 (recommendations and contract
//   notice periods), D17 (prices typed by Staff), D18 (manual holders and
//   usage), D21 (HR CSV import), D23 (reseller contracts). The tables they
//   used are kept but not written by the agreed use cases (D38).
//
// Decisions of the business model revision (2026-11-15), pending team
// confirmation:
//   D24. Organization tree of five fixed levels, group > P&L > block >
//        department > project (BR-21): org_units.level and code; the group is
//        the only unit without parent; units come from ILVG.
//   D25. User scope: user_org_units (was manager_org_units) lists the units of
//        a Manager, at any level, the group included, and the companies of a
//        Staff member (a P&L, or the group for group-level Staff) (BR-16).
//   D26. One usage connector per company and provider (connectors.org_unit_id,
//        vendor_id). A license_plans row is one license a connector reports:
//        its external name, license type, and connector.
//   D27. Owner unit (BR-26): the P&L of the connector, or the group for a
//        shared license (used by two or more companies); a license reported by
//        two connectors is counted once (license_plans.duplicate_of_id).
//   D28. Software catalog mapping (BR-38): license_plans.product_id NULL =
//        Not mapped; a product has one category.
//   D29. Budget versions (BR-08): each confirmed import is a budget_plans
//        version for a target unit and months; its lines belong to the deepest
//        unit they name, per license and month; the lines it replaces get
//        superseded_at (which lines: D42). A shared license is planned by the
//        group, one line per P&L (BR-26).
//   D30. Idempotent budget import (BR-36): one preview_key per preview, the
//        latest version seen at preview (based_on_budget_plan_id, D43), and the
//        unchanged status when the file changes nothing.
//   D31. Seat status over 30 days with a 30-day grace for new seats (BR-03);
//        usage frequency = days used against working days, from active_days
//        usage records, without bands (BR-35).
//   D32. Cost split into used, wasted, and not evaluated (BR-24) on
//        cost_allocations; unassigned seats go to unallocated under the owner
//        unit, unplaced holders to unknown_unit (BR-06, BR-21).
//   D33. Purchased = accrued cost of the invoices (BR-09, UC42): an expense
//        names the term it pays for (service_from, service_to) and keeps its
//        monthly spread (accrual_schedule), rounded to the thousand VND
//        (BR-25); months are closed per company.
//   D34. Connector sync interval and pause (BR-32): sync_interval_hours,
//        paused_at, reconfigured_at; a scheduled run while paused is a
//        sync_runs row with status paused.
//   D35. Account type of a provider identity: personal, shared, service
//        (BR-28); identities belong to the connector (tenant) that reports them.
//   D36. Employee application usage from BCA in its own table,
//        employee_app_usage (BR-23); the 40th table.
//   D37. BCA and ILVG are connectors too (connectors.kind), so their runs are
//        monitored like the usage connectors (UC26).
//   D38. Tables of retired use cases are kept, not written: contracts,
//        entitlement_allocations, product_links, recommendations.
//   D39. A holder on several projects counts toward each in equal parts and
//        not toward their own unit (BR-06): employees.project_ids, and seat
//        counts of plan_unit_daily_snapshots are shares (numeric).
//   D40. Deleting a connector (UC60) sets is_active false and keeps its data;
//        one active usage connector per company and provider.
//   D41. A shared or service account is judged as a whole account (BR-28):
//        its seat has a status like any other and its cost is Used or Wasted.
//
// Decisions of the schema review (2026-11-15), pending team confirmation:
//   D42. A budget import changes only the licenses in its file (BR-08): for
//        the target, every unit under it, and the months, each license of the
//        file replaces its own lines (a line of that license the file no
//        longer has is removed); licenses not in the file keep their lines. A
//        license of the file is its name plus the Shared column (D45).
//   D43. Concurrent budget imports (BR-36): based_on_budget_plan_id is the
//        latest version of any unit at preview; the confirm is refused when a
//        line of its scope was written or superseded by a later version, so an
//        import at the same unit, above, or below is caught. Confirms run one
//        at a time, so version ids follow commit order.
//   D44. The cost of a month is split by seat-days (BR-03, BR-06, BR-27):
//        each day carries cost / days in the month, split by the seats of that
//        day over max(purchased, assigned) seats, so an over-allocated license
//        spreads over its assigned seats and leaves nothing unallocated. A day
//        without complete seat data takes the seats of the nearest complete day
//        of the month (cost_allocations.filled_days). The cost of a day that
//        cannot be split — no complete day in the month, or Purchased quantity
//        Unknown — is Not evaluated under the owner.
//   D45. A P&L can hold its own license and a share of a shared license with
//        the same name: the budget file has a Shared column
//        (budget_plan_lines.is_shared) that tells which one a line plans.
//   D46. Owner change (UC47): closed months keep the owner they were computed
//        with; open months follow the new owner. An expense keeps the company
//        that paid it. A P&L month that carries the cost of a shared license
//        stays Provisional until the group's month is closed too (BR-31).
//   D47. The fiscal year is the calendar year: accounting_periods has no
//        fiscal_year.
//   D48. When ILVG no longer reports a unit, the sync marks it inactive even if
//        employees, current budget lines, or licenses remain, and the unit is
//        listed to Admin (UC20). Admin alone still cannot deactivate it.
//   D49. Connector status is computed per license (BR-32) from its own
//        collection_coverage, so a license added to a running connector is
//        Pending and a license that failed in a partial run is Failed.
//
// Conventions:
//   - Target DBMS: PostgreSQL 15+. Surrogate keys are bigint identity columns;
//     every table has a single-column id so audit_logs can point to any row.
//   - Money is numeric(18,2). Amounts from outside (prices, expenses, budget
//     lines) carry an ISO 4217 currency; figures ELMS computes (snapshots,
//     allocations, detection costs) are in the reporting currency and carry
//     none. Amounts in different currencies are only added through
//     exchange_rates (BR-05, D12).
//   - Quantities are numeric(20,4) because one column serves seats, sessions,
//     tokens, and cores.
//   - A NULL figure means Unknown and is never read as 0 (BR-04, A4). NULL has
//     no second meaning: "unlimited" is its own flag (is_unlimited). A sum with
//     one Unknown part is Unknown, never the sum of the known parts (PostgreSQL
//     SUM skips NULL, so totals must check for NULL parts first).
//   - Master data is never deleted, only marked inactive or ended (BR-15), so
//     no foreign key cascades on delete.
//   - Where a date or timestamp decides a state, there is no status column
//     beside it: the group is the unit without parent_id, a month is closed
//     once closed_at is set, a connector is paused while paused_at is set, a
//     budget line is current while superseded_at is NULL, and a detection
//     result is not evaluated / clear / flagged when flagged_qty is NULL / 0 /
//     more than 0.
//   - Where a row has an end date, the date alone says whether it is active
//     (entitlement_lines.valid_to, employees.left_on,
//     license_assignments.ended_on, user_accounts.disabled_at). End dates are
//     inclusive: the row is valid on its last day.
//   - Each daily figure has one owner table: Purchased quantity and list cost in
//     plan_daily_snapshots, seat counts in plan_unit_daily_snapshots, period
//     usage in usage_records, completeness in collection_coverage.
//     detection_results stores only the verdict.
//   - Confidence (BR-14, A9) is derived from the source, not stored:
//     api or log per subject = high; api or log aggregate, or import = medium;
//     manual = low.
//   - sync_run_id and import_batch_id on a row name the run or import that wrote
//     it last; source is the source of that write. Licenses, holders, and usage
//     come from connectors only (source api or log, enforced by the
//     chk_*_connector_only checks); import and manual remain for budget lines
//     and expenses.
//   - Connector messages live at the level they describe:
//       whole run failed           sync_runs.error_message
//       one plan, kind, and day    collection_coverage.error_code, error_message
//       one provider record        raw_records.normalize_error
//     Messages are stored without secrets (tokens, keys).
//   - Settings are not stored in the database: they are application settings
//     of the API and the worker. reporting_currency VND (D12),
//     inactivity_threshold_days 30 and new_seat_grace_days 30 (BR-03),
//     default_sync_interval_hours 6
//     (BR-32), month_close_day 10 (D14), raw_record_retention_days 180,
//     password_link_valid_hours 72 (D22), budget_preview_valid_minutes 60.
//   - updated_at is set by the application (or a trigger) on every update;
//     the default only covers the insert.
//   - Rules DBML cannot express are written in the table notes:
//       "Partial unique"  = a unique index with WHERE and/or NULLS NOT DISTINCT,
//                           to be created in the migration
//       "App rule"        = cross-table rule enforced in the service, inside the
//                           transaction that changes the data
// =============================================================================

Project elms {
  database_type: 'PostgreSQL'
  Note: '''
    Enterprise License Management System (ELMS).
    Read-only toward providers (BR-01): every table here holds data inside ELMS;
    nothing in this schema is written back to a provider.
  '''
}

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Enums
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

Enum permission_action {
  read
  write
}

Enum data_source {
  api [note: 'Collected by a connector from a provider API, ILVG, or BCA']
  log [note: 'Collected by a connector from logs (license server, VPN)']
  import [note: 'File imported by a user: budget plan (UC33), expenses (UC07)']
  manual [note: 'Typed in by Staff: expenses only (UC07)']
}

Enum org_level {
  group [note: 'The whole group; the only unit without parent (BR-21)']
  pnl [note: 'P&L (company, subsidiary); parent is the group']
  block [note: 'Block (division); parent is a P&L']
  department [note: 'Department; parent is a block']
  project [note: 'Project; parent is a department']
}

Enum connector_kind {
  usage [note: 'Usage connector of one company and provider (UC55): licenses, holders, usage, terms']
  ilvg [note: 'ILVG: employees and their units (system process)']
  bca [note: 'BCA: application usage of employees on company machines (BR-23)']
}

Enum connector_auth {
  api_key
  bearer_token
}

Enum license_type {
  monthly
  yearly
  usage_based [note: 'Paid by consumption; consumers instead of seats (UC61)']
}

Enum account_type {
  personal [note: 'One person']
  shared [note: 'Group mailbox or shared account: judged as a whole account, Active or Inactive like any seat, cost Used or Wasted (BR-28, D41)']
  service [note: 'Service or system account: same as shared (BR-28, D41)']
}
Enum vendor_kind {
  publisher [note: 'Makes the software; products belong to a publisher']
  reseller [note: 'Distributor, reseller, or CSP partner; can sign contracts, owns no product (D23)']
}

Enum license_archetype {
  allocation [note: 'Seat, named user, device']
  concurrent [note: 'Slot, floating, VPN session']
  metered [note: 'Token, request, credit, GB']
  capacity [note: 'Core, CPU, server, instance']
}

Enum commercial_term {
  pay_as_you_go
  monthly
  yearly
  multi_year
  prepaid_credit
  perpetual [note: 'Perpetual with maintenance; only maintenance counts as cost (BR-05)']
}

Enum data_kind {
  entitlement [note: 'Purchased quantity and validity']
  assignment [note: 'Who holds the license']
  usage [note: 'Activity, sessions, consumption, deployed units']
  expense [note: 'Billing data: expenses and invoices']
}

Enum import_kind {
  budget [note: 'Budget plan from the ELMS Excel template (UC33, BR-08)']
  expense [note: 'Expenses (UC07)']
}
Enum usage_granularity {
  per_subject [note: 'Usage known per user, device, project, or key']
  aggregate [note: 'Only totals; seats stay Not monitored and are never listed per user (A9, D7)']
}

Enum subject_type {
  user
  device
  project
  api_key
  other
}

Enum usage_metric {
  active_subjects [note: 'Allocation, aggregate source only: number of active users in the period']
  active_days [note: 'Allocation, per subject: days with activity in the period, for days used (BR-35)']
  peak_concurrent [note: 'Concurrent: peak simultaneous sessions in the period']
  consumption [note: 'Metered: tokens, requests, credits, GB consumed in the period']
  deployed_units [note: 'Capacity: units deployed at the end of the period']
}
Enum sync_trigger {
  scheduled
  manual
  backfill [note: 'History loaded on the first connection (A5)']
}

Enum run_status {
  running
  success
  partial [note: 'Some data collected; collection_coverage says which plans are complete']
  failed [note: 'Nothing written; figures of that day stay Unknown, never 0 (A4)']
  paused [note: 'Scheduled run of a paused connector: nothing read, the period stays Unknown (BR-32)']
}
Enum coverage_status {
  complete [note: 'All data of this kind for the plan and account was collected for the day']
  partial [note: 'Some pages or subjects missing; treated as Unknown by detection']
  failed [note: 'Nothing collected; Unknown']
}

Enum import_status {
  previewed [note: 'Parsed and validated; nothing written yet']
  confirmed [note: 'Rows written']
  rejected [note: 'At least one invalid row; whole file refused']
  unchanged [note: 'The file changes nothing (no row to add, change, or remove), for example the same file again: nothing written, no new version (BR-36)']
}
Enum cost_bucket {
  unit [note: 'Cost of the seats held by the people of a unit (BR-06)']
  unallocated [note: 'Cost of purchased seats nobody holds (Wasted) and cost that could not be split (Not evaluated), carried by the owner unit (P&L, or the group for a shared license)']
  unknown_unit [note: 'Cost of seats whose holder cannot be placed in a unit, carried by the owner unit (BR-21)']
}
Enum allocation_method {
  per_seat [note: 'Accrued cost split day by day over max(purchased, assigned) seats, by the seats of each day (seat-days, BR-06, D44)']
  per_usage [note: 'usage_based license: split by the consumption of subjects with a known unit']
  direct [note: 'Expense that names a unit goes to that unit']
  none [note: 'No seat data in the whole month: the cost stays with the owner (unallocated) as Not evaluated (BR-04, D44)']
}
Enum detection_check {
  unused [note: 'Unassigned seats (UC10)']
  inactive [note: 'Seats in Inactive or No activity (UC11)']
  overuse [note: 'Allocated above purchased (BR-07, BR-34)']
  leaver [note: 'Open seats of employees who left or of identities disabled at the provider (D20)']
}
// Retired with UC13 and UC14 (D38): kept for the recommendations table only.
Enum recommendation_type {
  reduce_seats
  downgrade_plan
  cancel
  reassign
}

Enum recommendation_status {
  proposed
  accepted
  rejected
  done
}

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 1. Organization and access (UC19-UC22, UC24, BR-16, BR-21)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

Table org_units {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  parent_id bigint [ref: > org_units.id, note: 'NULL only for the group; otherwise the unit one level up']
  level org_level [not null, note: 'group, pnl, block, department, or project (BR-21)']
  code varchar(50) [not null, unique, note: 'Unit code from ILVG; the key the budget file and connectors use (BR-08)']
  name varchar(200) [not null]
  is_active boolean [not null, default: true]
  sync_run_id bigint [ref: > sync_runs.id, note: 'ILVG run that wrote the unit last; NULL for the seeded group row']
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (parent_id, name) [unique, name: 'uq_org_units_parent_name']
    level
  }

  checks {
    `parent_id is null or parent_id <> id` [name: 'chk_org_units_not_own_parent']
    `(level = 'group') = (parent_id is null)` [name: 'chk_org_units_group_root']
  }

  Note: '''
    The organization in five fixed levels: group > P&L > block > department >
    project (BR-21, D24). A "unit" in the docs is one row of this table. Units
    come from ILVG (system process); Admin assigns Managers (UC20) and can
    correct a unit ILVG placed wrongly, with a reason, through data_overrides.
    Partial unique: one group row (unique on level where level = 'group').
    App rule: the parent of a unit is one level up (pnl -> group, block -> pnl,
    department -> block, project -> department), which also rules out cycles;
    Admin cannot mark inactive a unit with active employees, a current budget
    line, or licenses it owns; when ILVG no longer reports such a unit, the
    sync marks it inactive anyway and the unit is listed to Admin (computed:
    inactive units that still have any of these), who moves what is left
    (D48, UC20). Every figure of a unit is the sum of the units
    under it (BR-21); Unallocated and Unknown unit are buckets of
    cost_allocations under the owner unit, not rows here.
  '''
}
Table employees {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  employee_code varchar(50) [unique, note: 'ILVG employee id; the key that joins ILVG, BCA, and holder identities (BR-27)']
  full_name varchar(200) [not null]
  email varchar(320) [not null, unique, note: 'Current company email, stored lowercase; login email of the account']
  org_unit_id bigint [ref: > org_units.id, note: 'Unit of the employee at any level, from ILVG. NULL = Unknown unit (BR-21)']
  unit_since date [note: 'Day the employee joined org_unit_id; a transfer splits usage and cost on this day (BR-27)']
  project_ids bigint[] [note: 'Projects the employee works on, from ILVG, when more than one; a seat counts toward each in equal parts and not toward org_unit_id (BR-06, D39). NULL = org_unit_id only']
  left_on date [note: 'Last working day; NULL = still with the company (D20). Seats still held after it are flagged by the leaver check']
  source data_source [not null, default: 'api', note: 'api = ILVG sync; manual = created with an account by Admin before ILVG knows the person']
  sync_run_id bigint [ref: > sync_runs.id]
  import_batch_id bigint [ref: > import_batches.id]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    org_unit_id
    left_on
  }

  checks {
    `email = lower(email)` [name: 'chk_employees_email_lowercase']
    `(source in ('api', 'log')) = (sync_run_id is not null)` [name: 'chk_employees_sync_provenance']
    `(source = 'import') = (import_batch_id is not null)` [name: 'chk_employees_import_provenance']
  }

  Note: '''
    Directory of real employees (decision D2), loaded from ILVG. An employee
    may have no account, so provider identities of people without an ELMS
    account still match an employee and a unit.
    Cost allocation, data scope, and "Unknown unit" read org_unit_id here,
    never from the account. Only the current unit is kept (D9); past months
    keep their unit through the frozen snapshots and cost_allocations, and
    unit_since tells the day of a transfer (BR-27). Cost follows the unit of
    each day's snapshot (D44), so a transfer counts from the day ELMS receives
    it: when ILVG reports a transfer late, the days before stay with the old
    unit. An employee on several projects has them in project_ids: a seat
    they hold counts toward each project in equal parts, half a seat each for
    two, and nothing toward org_unit_id (BR-06, D39).
    The other emails of a person over time are the user subjects matched to
    this employee (subjects.employee_id), so one person holds licenses under
    several emails (UC23, UC61).
    App rule: every element of project_ids is an org_units row of level project.
    App rule: once left_on has passed, the account of the employee is disabled
    (same transaction when the day is already past, otherwise the daily job)
    (D14).
  '''
}
Table roles {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  code varchar(30) [not null, unique, note: 'ADMIN, MANAGER, STAFF, EMPLOYEE']
  name varchar(100) [not null]
  description text

  Note: 'The four fixed roles (BR-17). Seeded; UC21 changes the role of a user, not this list.'
}

Table permissions {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  feature_code varchar(60) [not null, note: 'One per row of the role x feature matrix, e.g. license_list, usage, budget_plan, connectors, software_catalog']
  action permission_action [not null]
  description text

  indexes {
    (feature_code, action) [unique, name: 'uq_permissions_feature_action']
  }

  Note: 'Catalogue of what can be granted: feature x (read | write) (UC22). Seeded.'
}

Table role_permissions {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  role_id bigint [not null, ref: > roles.id]
  permission_id bigint [not null, ref: > permissions.id]

  indexes {
    (role_id, permission_id) [unique, name: 'uq_role_permissions_role_permission']
  }

  Note: '''
    Permission matrix; permissions belong to roles, never to single users (BR-17).
    App rule: Employee cannot be granted price or cost features; the permission
    Admin needs to manage permissions cannot be removed (UC22). Every change is
    written to audit_logs with its reason.
  '''
}

Table user_accounts {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  employee_id bigint [not null, unique, ref: - employees.id, note: 'Every account belongs to one employee; login email = employees.email']
  role_id bigint [not null, ref: > roles.id, note: 'Exactly one role per account (BR-17)']
  password_hash varchar(255) [note: 'Hashed, never plain (BR-18). NULL until the user sets a first password through the one-time link; login is refused']
  password_token_hash char(64) [unique, note: 'SHA-256 of the one-time link that sets or resets the password (D22); NULL = no link open']
  password_token_expires_at timestamptz [note: 'End of validity of that link: created + password_link_valid_hours']
  failed_login_count int [not null, default: 0, note: 'Consecutive failures; reset on success']
  locked_until timestamptz [note: 'Set to now + 15 minutes after 5 failures in a row (BR-18)']
  last_login_at timestamptz
  disabled_at timestamptz [note: 'NULL = active. Set = disabled: cannot log in and open sessions are revoked (UC19); cleared on re-enable']
  created_by bigint [ref: > user_accounts.id]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    role_id
  }

  checks {
    `failed_login_count >= 0` [name: 'chk_user_accounts_failed_count']
    `(password_token_hash is null) = (password_token_expires_at is null)` [name: 'chk_user_accounts_password_token']
  }

  Note: '''
    Login accounts (UC19, UC21, UC24). Accounts are disabled, never deleted.
    First password and reset (D22): creating an account, or "reset password" by
    Admin, stores the hash of a new random token and shows the link once to
    Admin, who hands it to the user; no e-mail server is needed. Opening the
    link before it expires sets password_hash, clears the token, and resets
    failed_login_count and locked_until. A new link replaces the old one.
    App rule: the last active Admin cannot be disabled or lose the Admin role;
    an Admin cannot disable themselves (BR-17). An account of an employee whose
    left_on has passed cannot be re-enabled (D14). A role change away from
    MANAGER or STAFF removes the rows of the account in user_org_units.
    Disabling an account clears its open password link.
  '''
}

Table user_sessions {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  user_account_id bigint [not null, ref: > user_accounts.id]
  token_hash char(64) [not null, unique, note: 'SHA-256 of the session id kept in the HttpOnly, Secure cookie']
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  expires_at timestamptz [not null]

  indexes {
    user_account_id
    expires_at
  }

  checks {
    `expires_at > created_at` [name: 'chk_user_sessions_expiry']
  }

  Note: '''
    Server-side sessions, so disabling an account ends its open sessions at once
    (UC19, BR-18). A new session id is issued at login (no session fixation).
    Logout, disabling the account, and a role change delete the rows of the
    session; expired rows are purged by a daily job. Cookie sessions need
    CSRF protection (SameSite cookie plus a CSRF token on writes).
  '''
}

Table user_org_units {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  user_account_id bigint [not null, ref: > user_accounts.id]
  org_unit_id bigint [not null, ref: > org_units.id]

  indexes {
    (user_account_id, org_unit_id) [unique, name: 'uq_user_org_units_account_unit']
    org_unit_id
  }

  Note: '''
    Data scope of a Manager or a Staff member (BR-16, D25); was
    manager_org_units.
      MANAGER  the units they are responsible for, at any level, the group
               included (UC20); a unit covers everything under it
      STAFF    the companies they work on (UC19): a P&L, or the group for
               group-level Staff, who see every company and keep the software
               catalog and the shared licenses (UC01, UC47)
    Admin and Employee have no rows: Admin reads the group through the group
    overview and the dashboards; an Employee reads only their own licenses.
    Who assigned a row and when is in audit_logs.
    App rule: the account has the MANAGER or STAFF role; for STAFF the unit is
    a P&L or the group.
  '''
}
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 2. Software catalog and licenses (UC01, UC02, UC04, UC27, UC47, UC57)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

Table vendors {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  name varchar(200) [not null, unique]
  kind vendor_kind [not null, default: 'publisher', note: 'publisher or reseller (D23)']
  website varchar(500)
  support_contact varchar(500)
  is_active boolean [not null, default: true]
  created_by bigint [ref: > user_accounts.id]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  Note: '''
    Providers (UC02): Microsoft, Atlassian, Adobe... A usage connector reads
    one provider for one company (D26). Resellers (kind reseller, D23) are
    kept for the retired contracts and are not used by the agreed use cases.
    UC02 lists the providers that have licenses in the period; quantities are
    shown per license only, never added across licenses (BR-05).
    App rule: a provider with an active connector cannot be marked inactive;
    products and connectors belong to a publisher only.
  '''
}


Table software_categories {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  parent_id bigint [ref: > software_categories.id, note: 'NULL = category; set = subcategory of that category']
  name varchar(100) [not null]

  indexes {
    (parent_id, name) [unique, name: 'uq_software_categories_parent_name']
  }

  checks {
    `parent_id is null or parent_id <> id` [name: 'chk_software_categories_not_own_parent']
  }

  Note: '''
    Category and subcategory in a two-level tree, kept by group-level Staff
    in the software catalog (UC01, BR-38), e.g. Productivity > Office &
    Collaboration.
    Partial unique: category names are unique where parent_id is null.
    App rule: the parent of a subcategory is a category (parent_id is null);
    a category used by a product cannot be deleted.
  '''
}

Table software_products {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  vendor_id bigint [not null, ref: > vendors.id]
  category_id bigint [ref: > software_categories.id, note: 'Most specific node (subcategory if any). NULL is shown as Uncategorized']
  name varchar(200) [not null]
  description text
  is_active boolean [not null, default: true]
  created_by bigint [ref: > user_accounts.id]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (vendor_id, name) [unique, name: 'uq_software_products_vendor_name']
    category_id
  }

  Note: '''
    Software of the catalog (UC01, BR-38), e.g. Microsoft 365: the level the
    license names of every company map to, so the License Dashboard (UC15)
    and the analysis by software and category (UC44) count M365 E3 of company
    A and Microsoft 365 E3 of company B together.
    The migration makes the name unique case-insensitive (on lower(name)).
    App rule: a product with mapped licenses cannot be deleted, only merged
    into another product (its licenses are mapped to the other one, audited).
  '''
}

Table product_links {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  product_id bigint [not null, ref: > software_products.id]
  label varchar(100) [not null]
  url varchar(1000) [not null]

  indexes {
    product_id
  }

  Note: 'Useful links of a product: policy, terms of service, admin portal. Not used by the agreed use cases (D38).'
}

Table license_plans {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  connector_id bigint [not null, ref: > connectors.id, note: 'Usage connector that reports the license for its company (D26)']
  external_name varchar(200) [not null, note: 'License name as the source gives it, or as Staff typed it on the connector until the first sync (UC55)']
  external_ref varchar(200) [note: 'Id of the license at the source, e.g. Microsoft Graph skuId; NULL until the first sync']
  product_id bigint [ref: > software_products.id, note: 'Software of the catalog (UC01, BR-38). NULL = Not mapped, grouped under Uncategorized']
  license_type license_type [note: 'monthly, yearly, or usage_based as the source reports it (BR-02); NULL = Unknown until the first sync']
  archetype license_archetype [not null, default: 'allocation', note: 'How it is counted: seats (allocation), sessions, consumption, or capacity']
  unit varchar(30) [not null, default: 'seat', note: 'What is counted: seat, device, slot, token, credit, GB, core ...']
  owner_org_unit_id bigint [not null, ref: > org_units.id, note: 'Owner unit (D27): the P&L of the connector, or the group for a shared license (BR-26)']
  duplicate_of_id bigint [ref: > license_plans.id, note: 'Same license also reported by another connector, which Staff chose as the source (UC47): this row is counted nowhere']
  is_active boolean [not null, default: true, note: 'False once the connector no longer reports it, Staff removed it from the connector, or the connector was deleted (UC60)']
  created_by bigint [ref: > user_accounts.id]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    product_id
    owner_org_unit_id
    archetype
  }

  checks {
    `duplicate_of_id is null or duplicate_of_id <> id` [name: 'chk_license_plans_not_own_duplicate']
  }

  Note: '''
    The unit everything else calls "a license" (D1): one license a connector
    reports for its company, such as "Microsoft 365 E3" of company A. Staff
    declare it on the connector (UC55); it is Pending until the first sync
    (BR-32) and then carries the external_ref and license type of the source.
    Holders, usage, budget lines, and expenses point to it; it stays the same
    across renewals. Purchased = sum of its entitlement lines active on a day.
    Software and category (BR-38): product_id maps it to the catalog (UC01).
    Mapping one name maps every license of the same provider with the same
    name (lower(external_name)), in every company; a new name is Not mapped.
    Owner unit (D27, BR-26): the P&L of the connector's company; Staff set it to
    the group when the license is used by two or more companies (UC47). The
    owner carries the unassigned seats (cost_allocations unallocated) and plans
    the license; the cost of held seats is charged back to the holders' units.
    "Possibly shared" is computed: open seats held by employees of two or more
    P&Ls.
    Partial unique: one row per connector and name, case-insensitive (unique
    on connector_id, lower(external_name)), and one per connector and
    external_ref where external_ref is not null.
    App rule: owner_org_unit_id is the P&L of the connector or the group; a
    row with duplicate_of_id is left out of every figure; the vendor of
    product_id is the vendor of the connector; changing product_id or
    owner_org_unit_id is written to audit_logs (BR-15). Changing
    owner_org_unit_id recomputes the open months under the new owner; closed
    months keep the owner they were computed with (D46).
  '''
}
Table contracts {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  vendor_id bigint [not null, ref: > vendors.id, note: 'Party the contract is signed with: the publisher or a reseller (D23)']
  contract_no varchar(100) [note: 'Number on the vendor paper, if any']
  title varchar(200) [not null]
  start_date date [not null]
  renewal_date date
  notice_period_days int [note: 'Days before renewal_date the vendor must be told. NULL = Unknown, never read as 0 (BR-04, D16)']
  auto_renew boolean [not null, default: false]
  commitment_amount numeric(18,2) [note: 'Minimum commitment of the agreement, if any']
  total_value numeric(18,2)
  currency char(3)
  ended_on date [note: 'NULL = not ended. Set by "mark ended" (UC04)']
  notes text
  created_by bigint [ref: > user_accounts.id]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (vendor_id, contract_no) [unique, name: 'uq_contracts_vendor_no']
    renewal_date
    ended_on
  }

  checks {
    `renewal_date is null or renewal_date >= start_date` [name: 'chk_contracts_renewal_after_start']
    `ended_on is null or ended_on >= start_date` [name: 'chk_contracts_ended_after_start']
    `notice_period_days is null or notice_period_days >= 0` [name: 'chk_contracts_notice_period']
    `(total_value is null and commitment_amount is null) or currency is not null` [name: 'chk_contracts_currency']
    `commitment_amount is null or commitment_amount >= 0` [name: 'chk_contracts_commitment']
    `total_value is null or total_value >= 0` [name: 'chk_contracts_total_value']
  }

  Note: '''
    Retired (D38): contracts are no longer entered in ELMS; UC04 reads the
    license terms from entitlement_lines. The table is kept and not written.
    Former use: contracts (UC04). A contract is active on a day when start_date <= day and
    ended_on is null or later; there is no status column.
    Computed, not stored:
      Notice deadline       = renewal_date - notice_period_days: the last day to
                              tell the vendor before an auto-renewal (UC13);
                              Unknown when notice_period_days is NULL
      Renewal soon          = renewal_date within 30 days
      Notice period passed  = today > notice deadline
      Notice period unknown = auto_renew, renewal_date set, and
                              notice_period_days NULL: shown as a risk (UC17)
    Renewal dates feed the forecast (UC09) and recommendation timing (UC13).
    With an Unknown notice period, UC13 shows the action date as Unknown and
    never as "now".
    Files of a contract (agreement, amendments, PO) are files rows with
    contract_id set.
  '''
}

Table entitlement_lines {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  license_plan_id bigint [not null, ref: > license_plans.id]
  contract_id bigint [ref: > contracts.id, note: 'Retired (D38); always NULL']
  quantity numeric(20,4) [note: 'Purchased quantity of the term. NULL = Unknown, unless is_unlimited']
  is_unlimited boolean [not null, default: false, note: 'True for a term bought without a quota (e.g. usage-based pay-as-you-go): quantity is NULL and it can never be over-allocated (BR-07)']
  valid_from date [not null, note: 'Start of the term; when the source gives none, one year before valid_to (BR-33)']
  valid_to date [note: 'Expiry or renewal date, inclusive. NULL = open-ended']
  auto_renew boolean [note: 'As the source reports it; NULL = not reported, shown as "-" (UC04)']
  commercial_term commercial_term [not null, note: 'How the term is paid; it also fixes the period of unit_price']
  unit_price numeric(18,4) [note: 'List price of price_per_qty units for the period of the commercial term, as the source reports it. NULL = Unknown']
  price_per_qty numeric(20,4) [not null, default: 1, note: 'How many units unit_price is quoted for: 1 for a seat, 1000000 for "2.50 USD per 1M tokens"']
  currency char(3) [not null]
  source data_source [not null, default: 'api', note: 'Source of the row (BR-14): a connector']
  external_ref varchar(200) [note: 'Subscription or term id at the source']
  sync_run_id bigint [ref: > sync_runs.id]
  import_batch_id bigint [ref: > import_batches.id]
  created_by bigint [ref: > user_accounts.id]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (license_plan_id, valid_from, valid_to)
    valid_to
  }

  checks {
    `quantity is null or quantity >= 0` [name: 'chk_entitlement_lines_quantity']
    `not is_unlimited or quantity is null` [name: 'chk_entitlement_lines_unlimited']
    `valid_to is null or valid_to >= valid_from` [name: 'chk_entitlement_lines_validity']
    `unit_price is null or unit_price >= 0` [name: 'chk_entitlement_lines_unit_price']
    `price_per_qty > 0` [name: 'chk_entitlement_lines_price_per_qty']
    `source in ('api', 'log')` [name: 'chk_entitlement_lines_connector_only']
    `(source in ('api', 'log')) = (sync_run_id is not null)` [name: 'chk_entitlement_lines_sync_provenance']
    `(source = 'import') = (import_batch_id is not null)` [name: 'chk_entitlement_lines_import_provenance']
  }

  Note: '''
    One term or purchase of a license as its connector reports it: quantity,
    validity, auto-renew, and list price. It gives Purchased quantity
    (UC57, BR-34), the license terms (UC04), and the expiry (BR-33, UC58).
    A renewal or an extra purchase is a new line under the same license.
    A line is active on a day when valid_from <= day and (valid_to is null or
    valid_to >= day). A renewal starts the day after the previous line ends,
    so the boundary day is never counted twice.
    The list monthly cost (License List, open decision 19) is computed from
    unit_price / price_per_qty and the commercial term and frozen daily in
    plan_daily_snapshots. Purchased in money is the accrued cost of the
    expenses (D33, cost_allocations), not this price.
    Partial unique: one line per term at the source (unique on
    license_plan_id, external_ref where external_ref is not null), so a re-run
    sync updates the line instead of adding one (A3, BR-36).
  '''
}
Table entitlement_allocations {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  entitlement_line_id bigint [not null, ref: > entitlement_lines.id]
  org_unit_id bigint [not null, ref: > org_units.id]
  quantity numeric(20,4) [not null]
  valid_from date [not null, note: 'First day of the quota; on or after the valid_from of the line']
  valid_to date [note: 'Last day, inclusive. NULL = until the line ends (D19)']
  created_by bigint [ref: > user_accounts.id]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (entitlement_line_id, org_unit_id, valid_from) [unique, name: 'uq_entitlement_allocations_line_unit_from']
    org_unit_id
  }

  checks {
    `quantity > 0` [name: 'chk_entitlement_allocations_quantity']
    `valid_to is null or valid_to >= valid_from` [name: 'chk_entitlement_allocations_validity']
  }

  Note: '''
    Retired (D38): quotas per unit are not in the agreed use cases; the cost of
    a license goes to the units of its holders (BR-06). Kept, not written.
    Former use: optional quota of a purchase per unit (decision D3); gives the "Purchased"
    level per unit in budget monitoring (UC08, BR-09) and the unit of its
    unassigned seats (D10).
    A line with no rows is shared: its seats belong to the owner unit of the
    plan for detection, and no "Unassigned" gap is flagged per unit (BR-04).
    Quotas have their own validity (D19): moving 5 seats from unit A to unit B
    in the middle of a line ends the two current rows the day before and adds
    two new rows from that day. A quota row is active on a day like a line.
    A renewal line copies the quotas in force on the last day of the renewed
    line; a synced subscription keeps its line across renewals, so its quotas
    carry on. History per day is kept in plan_unit_daily_snapshots.
    App rule: quotas are allowed only on a line with a known quantity that is
    not unlimited; on every day the active quotas of a line add up to at most
    its quantity, and the rows of one line and unit never overlap. The service
    locks the line row (SELECT ... FOR UPDATE) before checking, so two
    concurrent changes cannot exceed it.
  '''
}

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 3. Collection pipeline (UC26, UC33, UC38, UC55, UC56, UC60, UC07 imports)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

Table connectors {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  kind connector_kind [not null, default: 'usage', note: 'usage connector of a company and provider, or the ILVG or BCA source (D37)']
  org_unit_id bigint [ref: > org_units.id, note: 'Company of a usage connector: a P&L, or the group for a group contract. NULL for ILVG and BCA']
  vendor_id bigint [ref: > vendors.id, note: 'Provider a usage connector reads. NULL for ILVG and BCA']
  name varchar(200) [not null, unique, note: 'Generated: "<Company> - <Provider> Usage" (UC55)']
  connector_type varchar(60) [not null, note: 'Implementation key, e.g. generic_rest, ms_graph, ilvg, bca']
  api_url varchar(500) [not null, note: 'Full HTTPS address of the endpoint the P&L provides for its own data (UC55), e.g. https://api.company.com/v1/usage']
  auth_type connector_auth [not null, note: 'API key or bearer token (UC55)']
  credentials_ref text [not null, note: 'Reference to the secret in the secret store, or the credential encrypted with a key kept outside the database; write-only, never shown, exported, or logged (BR-20)']
  contact_name varchar(100) [note: 'API contact of the company; required for a usage connector (UC55)']
  contact_email varchar(160) [note: 'Email of the API contact; required for a usage connector']
  sync_interval_hours int [not null, default: 6, note: 'How often the connector runs, typed freely by Staff, at least 1 (BR-32, UC55, UC60)']
  reconfigured_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`, note: 'Last change of company, provider, authentication, or API URL: every license is Pending again and runs before it no longer count (BR-32)']
  paused_at timestamptz [note: 'NULL = running; set = paused by Staff (UC26): scheduled runs are written with status paused']
  paused_by bigint [ref: > user_accounts.id]
  is_simulated boolean [not null, default: false, note: 'True when the connector reads a fake provider, so figures are labelled mock (BR-14)']
  is_active boolean [not null, default: true, note: 'False once deleted by Staff (UC60): no more runs; its licenses become inactive and the data collected stays (BR-15)']
  created_by bigint [ref: > user_accounts.id]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    org_unit_id
    vendor_id
  }

  checks {
    `(kind = 'usage') = (org_unit_id is not null and vendor_id is not null)` [name: 'chk_connectors_usage_target']
    `kind <> 'usage' or (contact_name is not null and contact_email is not null)` [name: 'chk_connectors_usage_contact']
    `sync_interval_hours > 0` [name: 'chk_connectors_interval']
    `(paused_at is null) = (paused_by is null)` [name: 'chk_connectors_paused']
    `api_url like 'https://%'` [name: 'chk_connectors_https']
  }

  Note: '''
    One read-only connection (D26, D37). A usage connector reads one provider
    for one company and answers in the license data contract (BR-19); its
    licenses are the license_plans rows with its connector_id. ILVG and BCA are
    connectors of their own kind, so every source is monitored the same way
    (UC26).
    Status of each license of a connector (BR-32, D49), computed, not stored,
    from the runs after reconfigured_at and the collection_coverage rows of
    the license they wrote:
      Paused   paused_at is set
      Pending  no coverage row of the license from a run after
               reconfigured_at (also a license added to a running connector)
      Failed   the latest finished run failed as a whole, or the latest
               coverage row of the license is failed
      Delayed  the latest run that wrote a complete or partial coverage row
               of the license is older than sync_interval_hours
      Active   otherwise
    Paused slots are left out of "latest run". Sync issues = Delayed + Failed.
    Partial unique: one active usage connector per company and provider
    (unique on org_unit_id, vendor_id where kind = 'usage' and is_active), so a
    deleted connector can be created again; one ILVG and one BCA connector
    (unique on kind where kind <> 'usage').
    App rule: a connection is saved only after its test passes (BR-20);
    editing company, provider, authentication, or API URL sets reconfigured_at
    and requires a new credential when provider or authentication changes
    (UC60); the interval and the licenses can change without it. Pause and
    resume are written to audit_logs (BR-15). Delete (UC60, D40) sets
    is_active false on the connector and its licenses in one transaction,
    after a confirmation; nothing is removed.
  '''
}
Table plan_data_sources {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  license_plan_id bigint [not null, ref: > license_plans.id]
  data_type data_kind [not null]
  source_type data_source [not null, default: 'api', note: 'Stamped as source on every row collected for this plan and kind of data']
  external_ref varchar(200) [note: 'Key of the plan in this kind of data when it differs from license_plans.external_ref, e.g. the product name a usage report uses; NULL = the same']
  granularity usage_granularity [note: 'Required for usage: per subject or aggregate only']
  has_daily_activity boolean [note: 'Usage per subject: true when the source gives activity per day (active_days), false when it gives only the last activity date, so frequency is Not tracked (BR-35)']
  monitoring_since date [not null, default: `current_date`, note: 'First day this source delivered data; Inactive needs 30 days of monitoring (BR-03)']
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (license_plan_id, data_type) [unique, name: 'uq_plan_data_sources_plan_type']
  }

  checks {
    `source_type in ('api', 'log')` [name: 'chk_plan_data_sources_connector_only']
    `(data_type = 'usage') = (granularity is not null)` [name: 'chk_plan_data_sources_granularity']
    `has_daily_activity is null or (data_type = 'usage' and granularity = 'per_subject')` [name: 'chk_plan_data_sources_daily_activity']
  }

  Note: '''
    Which kinds of data the connector of a plan delivers, and how (BR-14).
    Licenses, holders, and usage come from connectors only (BR-01).
    - A plan with no "usage" row, or with an aggregate one, has no per-seat
      usage: its seats are "Not monitored" (BR-03, D7) and are never counted as
      waste (BR-04, BR-24).
    - has_daily_activity false: seat status is computed from the last activity
      date, frequency is Not tracked (BR-35).
    The connector is the one of the plan (license_plans.connector_id); it is
    not copied here, so the two cannot disagree.
  '''
}
Table sync_runs {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  connector_id bigint [not null, ref: > connectors.id]
  trigger sync_trigger [not null, default: 'scheduled', note: 'scheduled, manual (run now or rerun a period, UC26), or backfill']
  status run_status [not null, default: 'running']
  data_date date [not null, note: 'The day the collected figures describe (reports lag 1-2 days); the period a rerun replaces']
  window_start timestamptz [note: 'Incremental window (A3)']
  window_end timestamptz
  error_message text [note: 'Only when the whole run failed (bad credentials, provider unreachable); errors of one plan are in collection_coverage']
  started_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  finished_at timestamptz

  indexes {
    (connector_id, data_date)
    status
  }

  checks {
    `(status = 'running') = (finished_at is null)` [name: 'chk_sync_runs_finished']
    `finished_at is null or finished_at >= started_at` [name: 'chk_sync_runs_duration']
    `window_end is null or window_start is null or window_end >= window_start` [name: 'chk_sync_runs_window']
    `(status = 'failed') = (error_message is not null)` [name: 'chk_sync_runs_error']
    `status <> 'paused' or finished_at = started_at` [name: 'chk_sync_runs_paused']
  }

  Note: '''
    One execution of a connector, or one scheduled slot of a paused connector
    (status paused, nothing read, BR-32), so the run table of UC26 shows the
    pause like any run. A failed or paused run writes no figures, so that day
    stays Unknown instead of 0 (A4, BR-04); the next run catches up (A3). A
    rerun of the same connector and data date replaces the figures and never
    duplicates them (BR-36).
    Which plans a run covered completely is in collection_coverage.
    A backfill writes one run per data date.
    What a run returned is found through sync_run_id: its raw payloads in
    raw_records, the rows it wrote last in the normalized tables, and its
    coverage rows. Record counts are not stored: they are counted from those
    tables while the raw records are kept.
  '''
}

Table collection_coverage {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  license_plan_id bigint [not null, ref: > license_plans.id]
  data_type data_kind [not null]
  data_date date [not null]
  status coverage_status [not null]
  sync_run_id bigint [not null, ref: > sync_runs.id, note: 'Latest run that wrote this day']
  error_code varchar(60) [note: 'Why the day is not complete, e.g. permission_denied, anonymized_report, timeout, contract_violation']
  error_message text [note: 'Message returned by the provider for this plan and kind, without secrets']
  collected_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (license_plan_id, data_type, data_date) [unique, name: 'uq_collection_coverage_plan_type_date']
    (data_date, status)
    sync_run_id
  }

  checks {
    `(status = 'complete') = (error_code is null)` [name: 'chk_collection_coverage_error']
  }

  Note: '''
    Whether the data of a plan and kind is complete for a day
    (decision D8). A connector run writes one row per plan and kind it
    collects; a later run of the same day replaces the row.
    No row, partial, or failed = Unknown for that day: detection reports
    not_evaluated (UC10, UC11, UC35) and daily snapshots are not written.
    A successful run that finds 0 holders writes complete, so a true 0 is
    told apart from a missing day. Data the provider returns but ELMS cannot
    use is not complete: a usage report with anonymized user names, or
    signInActivity refused for lack of an Entra ID plan, is failed with its
    error_code.
    A record that fails the license data contract validator is rejected with
    its reason (BR-19): the day is partial, or failed when nothing passes.
  '''
}

Table raw_records {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  sync_run_id bigint [not null, ref: > sync_runs.id]
  record_type varchar(60) [not null, note: 'Provider object, e.g. subscribedSku, user, activeUserDetail']
  external_id varchar(200)
  payload jsonb [not null]
  fetched_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  normalized_at timestamptz [note: 'NULL until processed; set also when the record failed or was skipped']
  normalize_error varchar(200) [note: 'NULL = written to the tables below. Otherwise why not, e.g. undeclared_license, invalid_date, missing_field (BR-19)']

  indexes {
    (sync_run_id, record_type)
    (record_type, external_id)
  }

  checks {
    `normalize_error is null or normalized_at is not null` [name: 'chk_raw_records_normalize_error']
  }

  Note: '''
    Raw provider data kept before normalization, so rules can change and be
    recomputed without calling the API again (A2). Only successful responses
    are stored; a failed call is reported in collection_coverage or sync_runs.
    A record ELMS cannot use keeps its reason in normalize_error; the
    rejected records of a run, with the check that failed, are what Staff see
    in UC26. A license the source reports but the connector does not declare
    is undeclared_license, listed for Staff to add to the connector (UC60), so
    no purchase is silently left out.
    A normalized row points to the run that wrote it (sync_run_id), not to
    its raw record: raw records are deleted after the retention period. The
    raw record of a row is found by sync_run_id and external_id.
    Payloads hold personal data (names, emails): only the collection service
    reads this table, and rows older than raw_record_retention_days
    (application setting) are deleted. Idempotency is ensured by the unique
    keys of the normalized tables.
  '''
}

Table files {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  storage_key varchar(500) [not null, unique, note: 'Path or object key in file storage; the bytes are not in the database']
  original_name varchar(255) [not null]
  content_type varchar(100) [not null]
  size_bytes bigint [not null]
  checksum char(64) [not null, note: 'SHA-256 of the content; tells the same file uploaded again in the import history']
  contract_id bigint [ref: > contracts.id, note: 'Retired (D38); always NULL']
  uploaded_by bigint [ref: > user_accounts.id]
  uploaded_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    contract_id
  }

  checks {
    `size_bytes > 0 and size_bytes <= 10485760` [name: 'chk_files_size']
  }

  Note: '''
    Uploaded files: expense invoices (PDF or image, at most 10 MB, BR-10),
    budget plan Excel files (UC33), and CSV expense files. A budget file that
    changes nothing is told by its preview, not by checksum (BR-36). The service
    checks the content type from the bytes, not from the name; files are
    served only through the API with the permission of the row they belong to.
  '''
}

Table import_batches {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  import_type import_kind [not null]
  file_id bigint [not null, ref: > files.id]
  target_org_unit_id bigint [ref: > org_units.id, note: 'Budget: the unit where, with every unit under it, the file changes the licenses it names (BR-08, D42)']
  period_from date [note: 'Budget: first day of the first month the file covers']
  period_to date [note: 'Budget: first day of the last month the file covers']
  preview_key uuid [not null, unique, note: 'Idempotency key of the confirm: a second confirm of the same key returns the first result (BR-36)']
  based_on_budget_plan_id bigint [ref: > budget_plans.id, note: 'Budget: the latest version of any unit when the preview was made (NULL = none yet); confirm is refused if a later version wrote or superseded a line of the import scope (BR-36, D43)']
  budget_plan_id bigint [unique, ref: - budget_plans.id, note: 'Budget: the version the confirm created']
  status import_status [not null, default: 'previewed']
  rows_total int [not null, default: 0]
  rows_added int [not null, default: 0]
  rows_updated int [not null, default: 0, note: 'Rows whose line in force has another quantity, amount, or currency']
  rows_removed int [not null, default: 0, note: 'Budget: lines in force of the file licenses, in the target and under it, that the file no longer has (UC33, D42)']
  rows_rejected int [not null, default: 0]
  error_report jsonb [note: 'Rejected rows with their reasons']
  imported_by bigint [not null, ref: > user_accounts.id]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  confirmed_at timestamptz

  indexes {
    (import_type, created_at)
    (target_org_unit_id, period_from)
  }

  checks {
    `(status = 'confirmed') = (confirmed_at is not null)` [name: 'chk_import_batches_confirmed']
    `(import_type = 'budget') = (target_org_unit_id is not null and period_from is not null and period_to is not null)` [name: 'chk_import_batches_budget_target']
    `period_to is null or period_to >= period_from` [name: 'chk_import_batches_period']
    `(budget_plan_id is not null) = (import_type = 'budget' and status = 'confirmed')` [name: 'chk_import_batches_budget_version']
    `rows_total >= 0 and rows_added >= 0 and rows_updated >= 0 and rows_removed >= 0 and rows_rejected >= 0` [name: 'chk_import_batches_counts']
  }

  Note: '''
    One import: preview, then confirm (UC33 budget, UC07 expenses). This is
    the import history "who, when, file, target, months, rows".
    Budget import (BR-08, BR-36, D29, D30, D42, D43):
    - scope of the import = the target and every unit under it, x the months,
      x the licenses of the file (name and Shared column, D45). Licenses not
      in the file and units outside the target are never touched.
    - preview: parse the file, check every row (unit codes in the hierarchy
      and inside the target subtree, one row per unit, license, Shared, and
      month), compare with the lines in force of the scope, and count rows to
      add (no line in force), replace (another quantity, amount, or
      currency), remove (a line in force of the scope the file no longer
      has), and reject; store based_on = the latest budget_plans id of any
      unit (NULL when there is none).
    - nothing to add, replace, or remove -> status unchanged, "No changes",
      no version (the same file again ends here).
    - confirm: in one transaction, take the budget import lock (confirms run
      one at a time, so version ids follow commit order); refuse when a line
      of the scope has budget_plan_id or superseded_by_plan_id greater than
      based_on, or any value when based_on is NULL ("The plan changed since
      your preview"), so an import at the same unit, above, or below that
      touched the same licenses and months is caught; create the
      budget_plans version; supersede the lines it
      replaces or removes; insert the added and replaced lines; set
      budget_plan_id. Lines that do not change stay as they are.
      A second confirm with the same preview_key returns this result again.
    - a preview older than budget_preview_valid_minutes must be made again.
    App rule: the target is one of the importer's units or under one
    (user_org_units, BR-16).
  '''
}
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 4. Holders, usage, and history (UC10, UC11, UC23, UC32, UC61, Usage screen)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

Table subjects {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  connector_id bigint [not null, ref: > connectors.id, note: 'Connector (company tenant) the identity lives at; identities are unique per connector (D35)']
  subject_type subject_type [not null, default: 'user']
  account_type account_type [not null, default: 'personal', note: 'personal, shared (group mailbox), or service (BR-28)']
  identifier varchar(320) [not null, note: 'Provider identity, lowercase: email / userPrincipalName, device name, project, key label']
  external_id varchar(200) [note: 'Immutable id at the provider, if any; survives a rename of the identifier']
  display_name varchar(200)
  employee_id bigint [ref: > employees.id, note: 'Personal user subjects: the ILVG employee, by employee id or email (BR-27). NULL = Unknown employee']
  org_unit_id bigint [ref: > org_units.id, note: 'Shared and service accounts, projects, keys: the unit that owns them (BR-28)']
  is_enabled boolean [note: 'Account enabled at the provider; NULL = Unknown. False with an open seat is flagged by the leaver check (D20)']
  source data_source [not null, default: 'api']
  sync_run_id bigint [ref: > sync_runs.id]
  import_batch_id bigint [ref: > import_batches.id]
  first_seen_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (connector_id, subject_type, identifier) [unique, name: 'uq_subjects_connector_type_identifier']
    employee_id
    org_unit_id
  }

  checks {
    `source in ('api', 'log')` [name: 'chk_subjects_connector_only']
    `employee_id is null or org_unit_id is null` [name: 'chk_subjects_one_unit_source']
    `subject_type = 'user' or employee_id is null` [name: 'chk_subjects_employee_only_user']
    `account_type = 'personal' or employee_id is null` [name: 'chk_subjects_shared_no_employee']
    `identifier = lower(identifier)` [name: 'chk_subjects_identifier_lowercase']
    `(source in ('api', 'log')) = (sync_run_id is not null)` [name: 'chk_subjects_sync_provenance']
    `(source = 'import') = (import_batch_id is not null)` [name: 'chk_subjects_import_provenance']
  }

  Note: '''
    Who or what holds a license at the provider: a user account, a device, a
    project, an API key. Kept apart from employees because a provider identity
    may match no employee (UC61 "Unknown employee").
    Holder identity (system process, BR-27): a personal user subject is matched
    to the ILVG employee by employee id, otherwise by email; one employee can
    have several subjects (old and new emails, several companies' tenants).
    Unit of a subject = employees.org_unit_id for a matched person, otherwise
    subjects.org_unit_id, otherwise Unknown unit.
    Holder moved (BR-27) is computed: an open seat on a subject whose employee
    now belongs to another P&L than the license owner, or on an email the
    employee no longer uses.
    Partial unique: unique on connector_id, external_id where external_id
    is not null; a sync matches on external_id first, so a renamed user keeps
    the same subject and seat history.
  '''
}
Table license_assignments {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  license_plan_id bigint [not null, ref: > license_plans.id]
  subject_id bigint [not null, ref: > subjects.id]
  assigned_on date [note: 'Assigned date reported by the provider; NULL = Unknown, then created_at counts']
  ended_on date [note: 'NULL = currently assigned']
  last_active_at timestamptz [note: 'Last recorded activity; NULL = no activity recorded. Only filled from a per-subject usage source']
  source data_source [not null, default: 'api']
  sync_run_id bigint [ref: > sync_runs.id]
  import_batch_id bigint [ref: > import_batches.id]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (license_plan_id, ended_on)
    subject_id
    last_active_at
  }

  checks {
    `ended_on is null or assigned_on is null or ended_on >= assigned_on` [name: 'chk_license_assignments_dates']
    `source in ('api', 'log')` [name: 'chk_license_assignments_connector_only']
    `(source in ('api', 'log')) = (sync_run_id is not null)` [name: 'chk_license_assignments_sync_provenance']
    `(source = 'import') = (import_batch_id is not null)` [name: 'chk_license_assignments_import_provenance']
  }

  Note: '''
    A holder of a license: "Assigned" data read from the connector; ELMS never
    assigns or revokes (BR-01). An ended assignment keeps its row.
    Partial unique: one open assignment per plan and subject
    (unique on license_plan_id, subject_id where ended_on is null).
    App rule: the subject belongs to the connector of the plan
    (subjects.connector_id = license_plans.connector_id).
    Seat status (BR-03, D31) is computed, not stored, for an open assignment,
    on the data date D. S = the usage source of the plan, T =
    inactivity_threshold_days (30), G = new_seat_grace_days (30), held =
    D - (assigned_on, or created_at when unknown):
      Not monitored = no S, or S.granularity = aggregate
      Active        = last_active_at within the last T days, or held < G days
                      and never used (grace period)
      Inactive      = last_active_at older than T days
      No activity   = last_active_at is null and held >= G days
    A shared or service account (subjects.account_type) is judged as a whole
    account the same way: used by anyone in the last T days = Active (BR-28).
    Usage frequency (BR-35), computed, without bands: days used = sum of
    active_days usage_records of the subject and plan over the period, shown
    against working days = Monday to Friday without public holidays from the
    later of the period start and assigned_on; Not tracked when
    S.has_daily_activity is not true.
    Detection (UC11) flags Inactive and No activity only when the usage
    coverage of D is complete and S.monitoring_since is at least T days old.
    Unassigned = purchased quantity minus open assignments.
  '''
}
Table usage_records {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  license_plan_id bigint [not null, ref: > license_plans.id]
  subject_id bigint [ref: > subjects.id, note: 'NULL = aggregate figure for the whole plan']
  metric usage_metric [not null]
  period_start date [not null]
  period_end date [not null, note: 'Inclusive']
  quantity numeric(20,4) [not null]
  source data_source [not null]
  sync_run_id bigint [ref: > sync_runs.id]
  import_batch_id bigint [ref: > import_batches.id]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (license_plan_id, subject_id, metric, period_start, period_end) [unique, name: 'uq_usage_records_period']
    (license_plan_id, metric, period_start)
    subject_id
  }

  checks {
    `period_end >= period_start` [name: 'chk_usage_records_period']
    `quantity >= 0` [name: 'chk_usage_records_quantity']
    `source in ('api', 'log')` [name: 'chk_usage_records_connector_only']
    `metric <> 'active_subjects' or subject_id is null` [name: 'chk_usage_records_active_subjects_aggregate']
    `metric <> 'active_days' or (subject_id is not null and quantity <= period_end - period_start + 1)` [name: 'chk_usage_records_active_days']
    `metric not in ('active_subjects', 'active_days', 'peak_concurrent') or quantity = trunc(quantity)` [name: 'chk_usage_records_whole_counts']
    `(source in ('api', 'log')) = (sync_run_id is not null)` [name: 'chk_usage_records_sync_provenance']
    `(source = 'import') = (import_batch_id is not null)` [name: 'chk_usage_records_import_provenance']
  }

  Note: '''
    Usage per period for Concurrent, Metered, and Capacity plans, aggregate
    activity for Allocation plans without per-user data, and the active days of
    each holder for days used (active_days, BR-35). The last activity of
    a seat lives in license_assignments.last_active_at.
    A sync of the same period replaces the row (A3, BR-36): the unique index
    must be created with NULLS NOT DISTINCT so it also holds for aggregate rows,
    where subject_id is NULL.
    App rule: one period length per plan and metric (the period of
    the source, usually a day or a month) and no overlapping periods, so sums
    over periods never count a day twice. The metric matches the archetype of
    the plan (see the enum notes). The subject, when set, belongs to the
    connector of the plan.
    Metered overuse (D13) = sum of consumption over the validity of a line
    with a quota, compared with that quota.
    A missing period is Unknown, never 0 (BR-04).
  '''
}

Table plan_daily_snapshots {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  snapshot_date date [not null]
  license_plan_id bigint [not null, ref: > license_plans.id]
  purchased_qty numeric(20,4) [note: 'Sum of the entitlement lines active that day; NULL = Unknown (one active line Unknown makes the sum Unknown), or unlimited']
  is_unlimited boolean [not null, default: false, note: 'True when an active line of the plan is unlimited; purchased_qty is then NULL']
  effective_monthly_cost numeric(18,2) [note: 'List cost of a full month at the terms in force that day, in the reporting currency; NULL = Unknown (price or exchange rate missing)']
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (snapshot_date, license_plan_id) [unique, name: 'uq_plan_daily_snapshots_date_plan']
    license_plan_id
  }

  checks {
    `not is_unlimited or purchased_qty is null` [name: 'chk_plan_daily_snapshots_unlimited']
  }

  Note: '''
    Daily Purchased quantity and list monthly cost per plan, kept by ELMS
    because providers give no history and a sync overwrites the quantity of a
    line, so past days cannot be recomputed from entitlement_lines. Feeds the
    License List (UC57, monthly cost per open decision 19), trends, and the
    seat basis of cost_allocations. Purchased in money is the accrual (D33).
    Rows are frozen once written; a later rate or price correction changes only
    new days (D9, D12). Amounts are converted with the latest exchange rate
    whose effective_from is on or before the snapshot date.
    effective_monthly_cost is a monthly rate, not a daily amount: the cost of a
    month = sum over its days of effective_monthly_cost / days in the month.
    Never add up the daily rows as they are.
    Assigned and Used are not stored here, so each figure has one owner:
    seat counts are the sum over units of plan_unit_daily_snapshots; peak,
    consumption, and deployed units of non-seat plans are in usage_records.
    No row or a NULL column = Unknown for that day.
  '''
}

Table plan_unit_daily_snapshots {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  snapshot_date date [not null]
  license_plan_id bigint [not null, ref: > license_plans.id]
  org_unit_id bigint [ref: > org_units.id, note: 'Unit of the holders that day, at any level; NULL = Unknown unit']
  active_qty numeric(20,4) [not null, note: 'Seats Active (grace period included), as shares: a holder on two projects counts 0.5 in each (D39)']
  inactive_qty numeric(20,4) [not null]
  no_activity_qty numeric(20,4) [not null]
  not_monitored_qty numeric(20,4) [not null]
  shared_service_qty numeric(20,4) [not null, note: 'Of the four above: seats of shared and service accounts, listed apart (BR-28)']
  used_qty numeric(20,4) [note: 'usage_based plans: consumption attributed to the unit; NULL = Unknown']
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (snapshot_date, license_plan_id, org_unit_id) [unique, name: 'uq_plan_unit_daily_snapshots']
    (license_plan_id, snapshot_date)
    (org_unit_id, snapshot_date)
  }

  checks {
    `active_qty >= 0 and inactive_qty >= 0 and no_activity_qty >= 0 and not_monitored_qty >= 0` [name: 'chk_plan_unit_daily_snapshots_counts']
    `shared_service_qty between 0 and active_qty + inactive_qty + no_activity_qty + not_monitored_qty` [name: 'chk_plan_unit_daily_snapshots_shared']
  }

  Note: '''
    Daily seat status per license and unit: every assigned seat has one status
    (BR-03), so Assigned is the sum of active, inactive, no activity, and not
    monitored. Seats are shares: a holder on several projects counts toward
    each in equal parts (BR-06, D39), so the units still add up (BR-21).
    shared_service_qty is the part held by shared and service accounts, judged
    as whole accounts and listed apart (BR-28). The unit is the one of that
    day, so history keeps it after an employee moves (D9, BR-27).
    The rows of every day of a month are the seat basis of the month (D44):
    cost_allocations splits each day's share of the accrued cost with them
    into Used (active), Wasted (inactive + no activity, plus the unassigned
    seats of the owner), and Not evaluated (not monitored) (BR-24). The seat
    counts shown for a month are those of its last day (BR-03).
    The unique index needs NULLS NOT DISTINCT because org_unit_id may be NULL.
    Rows are written only for a day whose assignment coverage is complete
    (D8); counts have no default, so a missing day is no row, never a row of
    zeros.
  '''
}
Table employee_app_usage {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  employee_id bigint [ref: > employees.id, note: 'Employee BCA reports; NULL = BCA identity not matched (open decision 3)']
  bca_identity varchar(320) [not null, note: 'Identity BCA gives (machine user or email), lowercase']
  application_name varchar(200) [not null, note: 'Application as BCA names it']
  active_minutes int [note: 'Minutes the application was in use in the period, as assumed (open decision 6)']
  product_id bigint [ref: > software_products.id, note: 'Catalog software the application maps to, set by the mapping of UC01; NULL = not mapped']
  period_start date [not null]
  period_end date [not null, note: 'Inclusive']
  days_used int [not null, note: 'Days with use of the application in the period']
  last_used_at timestamptz
  source data_source [not null, default: 'api']
  sync_run_id bigint [not null, ref: > sync_runs.id, note: 'BCA run that wrote the row']
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (bca_identity, application_name, period_start, period_end) [unique, name: 'uq_employee_app_usage_period']
    (employee_id, period_start)
    product_id
  }

  checks {
    `period_end >= period_start` [name: 'chk_employee_app_usage_period']
    `days_used >= 0 and days_used <= period_end - period_start + 1` [name: 'chk_employee_app_usage_days']
    `active_minutes is null or active_minutes >= 0` [name: 'chk_employee_app_usage_minutes']
    `bca_identity = lower(bca_identity)` [name: 'chk_employee_app_usage_identity_lowercase']
    `source = 'api'` [name: 'chk_employee_app_usage_source']
  }

  Note: '''
    Employee usage of applications on company machines, from BCA (BR-23, D36):
    kept in its own table, separate from the license usage tables, so later
    services and functions can use it. Read by UC32, by the days used of UC61
    when the license has no usage of its own, and only by the Managers of the
    employee's units (BR-16).
    A member with no machine reporting to BCA has no row: "Not tracked",
    never "not used" (BR-04). Assumed until the BCA API is known (open
    decisions 3, 6): BCA reports per day the domain account of the user, which
    carries the ILVG employee code, and each application with its active
    minutes, the machines of one person added together; ELMS matches the
    employee by code, otherwise by email. A sync of the same period replaces
    the row (BR-36).
  '''
}
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 5. Budget, cost, and expenses (UC05-UC09, UC33, UC34, UC42, Usage screen)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

Table budget_plans {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  org_unit_id bigint [not null, ref: > org_units.id, note: 'Target unit of the import that created the version: the file changed the licenses it names in this unit and every unit under it (D42)']
  fiscal_year int [not null]
  period_from date [not null, note: 'First day of the first month replaced']
  period_to date [not null, note: 'First day of the last month replaced']
  version_no int [not null, note: '1, 2, 3 ... per target unit']
  note text
  created_by bigint [not null, ref: > user_accounts.id]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (org_unit_id, version_no) [unique, name: 'uq_budget_plans_unit_version']
    (org_unit_id, fiscal_year)
  }

  checks {
    `period_to >= period_from` [name: 'chk_budget_plans_period']
    `extract(year from period_from) = fiscal_year and extract(year from period_to) = fiscal_year` [name: 'chk_budget_plans_year']
    `extract(day from period_from) = 1 and extract(day from period_to) = 1` [name: 'chk_budget_plans_month_start']
    `version_no > 0` [name: 'chk_budget_plans_version']
  }

  Note: '''
    One version of the budget plan, created by one confirmed Excel import
    (UC33, BR-08, D29); its import is import_batches.budget_plan_id. Every
    Manager imports for their own units and any unit under them: the Manager
    of a P&L can replace the plan of the P&L and of each block; the Manager of
    a block only the block and what is under it.
    A version is never edited or deleted; earlier versions are kept for UC05
    "compare with the previous version". The plan in force is the current
    lines (budget_plan_lines.superseded_at NULL), whatever version wrote them:
    a version writes only the lines its import added or replaced (D42).
  '''
}
Table budget_plan_lines {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  budget_plan_id bigint [not null, ref: > budget_plans.id]
  org_unit_id bigint [not null, ref: > org_units.id, note: 'Deepest unit the line names (group, P&L, block, department, project), inside the target subtree. A shared license is planned per P&L; a group line plans its free seats (BR-26)']
  license_name varchar(200) [not null, note: 'License as written in the file']
  is_shared boolean [not null, default: false, note: 'Shared column of the file: true = the line plans the share of a shared license (owner the group); false = a license the P&L of the unit owns (D45)']
  license_plan_id bigint [ref: > license_plans.id, note: 'License the name and Shared column match (see the note); NULL = Not mapped (UC33)']
  month date [not null, note: 'First day of the month planned']
  planned_quantity numeric(20,4) [not null]
  planned_amount numeric(18,2) [not null]
  currency char(3) [not null]
  superseded_at timestamptz [note: 'NULL = in force; set when a later import replaced the target subtree for this month']
  superseded_by_plan_id bigint [ref: > budget_plans.id, note: 'Version that replaced the line']
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (budget_plan_id, org_unit_id, license_name, is_shared, month) [unique, name: 'uq_budget_plan_lines_version_row']
    (org_unit_id, month)
    license_plan_id
  }

  checks {
    `planned_quantity >= 0` [name: 'chk_budget_plan_lines_quantity']
    `planned_amount >= 0` [name: 'chk_budget_plan_lines_amount']
    `extract(day from month) = 1` [name: 'chk_budget_plan_lines_month_start']
    `(superseded_at is null) = (superseded_by_plan_id is null)` [name: 'chk_budget_plan_lines_superseded']
  }

  Note: '''
    The Plan figure (BR-09): one line per unit, license, and month, in
    quantity and amount, with source budget_excel (BR-14). A line belongs to
    the deepest unit it names, so a unit's Plan = its own lines + the Plan of
    the units under it and no line is counted twice (BR-08, BR-21).
    A plan is judged where it is set (BR-37): a license planned at a unit above
    the one being viewed is shown there as "Planned at <unit>" and left out of
    its variance.
    Partial unique: one line in force per unit, license, Shared, and month
    (unique on org_unit_id, lower(license_name), is_shared, month where
    superseded_at is null). The migration makes the version-row index
    case-insensitive too (lower(license_name)), so a file with "M365 E3" and
    "m365 e3" for the same unit and month is rejected in the preview.
    Shared licenses (BR-26): the Manager of the group plans one line per P&L
    that uses the license, or deeper, with Shared = yes, so each P&L's Plan
    includes its share and is compared with its charge-back; a group line
    plans the seats the group keeps free. P&L Managers can then change or add
    the lines of their units. A P&L can hold its own license and a share of a
    shared license with the same name; the Shared column tells them apart
    (D45).
    Mapping to license_plan_id, among active licenses that are not
    duplicates, by lower(external_name): is_shared false -> the license
    owned by the P&L of org_unit_id; is_shared true -> the license owned by
    the group. No match -> Not mapped; more than one -> the row is rejected in
    the preview.
    App rule: confirming an import supersedes, in the same transaction, only
    the lines in force of its scope that it replaces or removes, then inserts
    the added and replaced lines (D42, BR-36). A line of the group unit is a
    shared line. A line is never linked to a duplicate license
    (license_plans.duplicate_of_id).
  '''
}
Table cost_allocations {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  accounting_period_id bigint [not null, ref: > accounting_periods.id, note: 'Month of the owner unit of the license when the month was computed; a closed month keeps it after an owner change (D46)']
  license_plan_id bigint [not null, ref: > license_plans.id]
  bucket cost_bucket [not null]
  org_unit_id bigint [not null, ref: > org_units.id, note: 'unit: the unit of the holders; unallocated and unknown_unit: the owner unit of the license']
  method allocation_method [not null]
  basis_qty numeric(20,4) [note: 'Average seats of the bucket over the month = seat-days / days in the month (per_seat), or its consumption (per_usage); NULL for direct and none']
  filled_days int [note: 'per_seat: days of the month without complete seat data that took the seats of the nearest complete day of the month (D44); 0 = every day had its own data; NULL for the other methods']
  amount numeric(18,2) [note: 'Share of the accrued cost of the month (Purchased, D33), in the reporting currency; NULL = Unknown']
  used_amount numeric(18,2) [note: 'Part of amount for Active seats or consumption (BR-24)']
  wasted_amount numeric(18,2) [note: 'Part for Inactive and No activity seats; all of an unallocated row (BR-24)']
  not_evaluated_amount numeric(18,2) [note: 'Part for Not monitored seats and Unknown data (BR-04)']
  computed_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (accounting_period_id, license_plan_id, bucket, org_unit_id) [unique, name: 'uq_cost_allocations_period_plan_bucket_unit']
    (org_unit_id, accounting_period_id)
    license_plan_id
  }

  checks {
    `basis_qty is null or basis_qty >= 0` [name: 'chk_cost_allocations_basis']
    `((method = 'per_seat') = (filled_days is not null)) and (filled_days is null or filled_days between 0 and 31)` [name: 'chk_cost_allocations_filled_days']
    `amount is not null or (used_amount is null and wasted_amount is null and not_evaluated_amount is null)` [name: 'chk_cost_allocations_unknown']
    `amount is null or used_amount is null or wasted_amount is null or not_evaluated_amount is null or amount = used_amount + wasted_amount + not_evaluated_amount` [name: 'chk_cost_allocations_split']
    `bucket <> 'unallocated' or used_amount is null or used_amount = 0` [name: 'chk_cost_allocations_unallocated_unused']
  }

  Note: '''
    Purchased, Used, Wasted, and Not evaluated of a license for one month,
    split to units (UC06, BR-06, BR-09, BR-24, D32). Source of the Usage
    screen, the waste analysis, the financial dashboard, and variance.
    Cost of the month = the accrual of the expenses of the license for that
    month (expenses.accrual_schedule, D33).
    Split, by method:
      per_seat   day by day (seat-days, D44): each day carries cost / days in
                 the month, split over max(Purchased quantity, assigned
                 seats) of that day: each unit its held seats of that day
                 (plan_unit_daily_snapshots), unknown_unit the unplaced
                 holders, unallocated the unassigned seats under the owner
                 (the group for a shared license, BR-26) - none when more
                 seats are assigned than purchased (BR-34). A day without
                 complete seat data takes the rows of the nearest complete
                 day of the same month (the earlier one on a tie), counted in
                 filled_days. The cost of a day whose Purchased quantity is
                 Unknown goes to the unallocated row as Not evaluated (BR-04).
      per_usage  by the consumption of subjects with a known unit; the rest is
                 unknown_unit
      direct     an expense that names a unit goes to that unit
      none       no complete seat data in the whole month: one unallocated
                 row, all Not evaluated
    The rows of a license and month add up to its cost (UC06 result), and the
    units add up the hierarchy (BR-21). Charge-back of a shared license is the
    unit rows of the companies that hold its seats (BR-26).
    Rows of an open month are recomputed daily. Closing the month computes
    them once more in the same transaction; rows of a closed month are never
    recomputed (D9).
  '''
}
Table expenses {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  expense_date date [not null, note: 'Invoice or charge date; decides the closed month (BR-10)']
  service_from date [note: 'First day of the license term the expense pays for; NULL = the month of expense_date (D33)']
  service_to date [note: 'Last day of that term, inclusive']
  amount numeric(18,2) [not null, note: 'Negative only for a correcting entry']
  currency char(3) [not null]
  license_plan_id bigint [not null, ref: > license_plans.id]
  org_unit_id bigint [not null, ref: > org_units.id, note: 'Company that pays the invoice: the owner unit of the license when the expense is entered; it does not follow a later owner change (BR-10, D46)']
  description text
  invoice_file_id bigint [ref: > files.id]
  accrual_schedule jsonb [note: 'Monthly spread of the amount over the term, e.g. {"2026-01": 10000000, ...}; months of closed periods are frozen (BR-25, UC42)']
  source data_source [not null, default: 'manual']
  external_ref varchar(200) [note: 'Id of the billing record at the source, for idempotent sync (A3)']
  sync_run_id bigint [ref: > sync_runs.id]
  import_batch_id bigint [ref: > import_batches.id]
  created_by bigint [ref: > user_accounts.id]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    expense_date
    (license_plan_id, service_from)
    (org_unit_id, expense_date)
  }

  checks {
    `amount <> 0` [name: 'chk_expenses_amount_not_zero']
    `(service_from is null) = (service_to is null)` [name: 'chk_expenses_service_pair']
    `service_to is null or service_to >= service_from` [name: 'chk_expenses_service_term']
    `(source in ('api', 'log')) = (sync_run_id is not null)` [name: 'chk_expenses_sync_provenance']
    `(source = 'import') = (import_batch_id is not null)` [name: 'chk_expenses_import_provenance']
  }

  Note: '''
    Expenses and invoices (UC07): the billed view (D5), and the cost the
    accrual spreads, so the source of Purchased (D33). Amounts are converted
    to VND with the rate in force on expense_date (BR-05).
    Accrual (UC42, BR-25): the amount is spread over the months of
    service_from..service_to, by days for a month the term starts or ends in;
    monthly amounts are rounded to the thousand VND and the difference goes to the last
    month, so the schedule always adds up to the amount. A cost change in the
    middle of the term (top-up, downgrade) is a new expense from the change;
    a closed month is never respread, its difference goes to the next open
    month.
    A license term without an expense leaves its months with Purchased
    Unknown (BR-04).
    Partial unique: one row per billing record
    (unique on license_plan_id, external_ref where external_ref is not null).
    App rule: an expense is editable until its month is closed
    (accounting_periods of its company); afterwards only a correcting entry is
    allowed, dated in an open month.
  '''
}
Table accounting_periods {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  org_unit_id bigint [not null, ref: > org_units.id, note: 'Company whose month it is: a P&L, or the group for shared licenses']
  period_year int [not null, note: 'Calendar year, which is also the fiscal year (D47)']
  period_month int [not null]
  closed_at timestamptz [note: 'NULL = open, figures Provisional (BR-31); set = closed']
  closed_by bigint [ref: > user_accounts.id, note: 'NULL when closed by the system job']

  indexes {
    (org_unit_id, period_year, period_month) [unique, name: 'uq_accounting_periods_unit_month']
  }

  checks {
    `period_month between 1 and 12` [name: 'chk_accounting_periods_month']
  }

  Note: '''
    Months of each company and whether they are closed (UC42). A closed month
    locks its expenses (BR-10), freezes its accrual and cost_allocations (D9),
    and removes the Provisional mark of its figures (BR-31).
    Closing: Staff close the month of their company after reviewing the
    accrual (UC42); otherwise a system job closes month M on month_close_day
    of M+1 (D14). A closed month is never reopened; later changes are
    correcting entries.
    A P&L month shows Provisional while it is open, and also while the group
    month of a shared license charged to the P&L is still open (D46, BR-31).
    App rule: org_unit_id is a P&L or the group.
  '''
}
Table exchange_rates {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  from_currency char(3) [not null, note: 'Any currency but the reporting currency']
  rate numeric(18,8) [not null, note: '1 from_currency = rate units of the reporting currency']
  effective_from date [not null]
  declared_by bigint [ref: > user_accounts.id]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (from_currency, effective_from) [unique, name: 'uq_exchange_rates_currency_date']
  }

  checks {
    `rate > 0` [name: 'chk_exchange_rates_rate']
  }

  Note: '''
    Exchange rates entered by group-level Staff (UC62, BR-05, D12), always
    toward the reporting currency. An amount is converted with the rate in
    force on its invoice date.
    The rate of a day = the row with the latest effective_from on or before that
    day. Without a rate, converted figures are Unknown and amounts are shown per
    currency, never added (UC16).
    A corrected rate changes only figures not yet frozen; frozen snapshots and
    cost_allocations of closed months keep the rate they were computed with.
  '''
}

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 6. Optimization (UC10, UC11, UC18, UC35)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

Table detection_runs {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  data_date date [not null, note: 'Date of the data the run evaluated']
  inactivity_threshold_days int [not null, default: 30, note: 'Copied from the application setting so old results stay explainable (BR-03)']
  rule_version varchar(20) [not null, note: 'Version of the detection rules, e.g. 2026.11']
  status run_status [not null, default: 'running']
  started_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  finished_at timestamptz

  indexes {
    data_date
  }

  checks {
    `(status = 'running') = (finished_at is null)` [name: 'chk_detection_runs_finished']
    `status <> 'paused'` [name: 'chk_detection_runs_status']
  }

  Note: 'One daily detection run (BR-12). A re-run for the same data date adds a new run; screens read the latest successful run.'
}

Table detection_results {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  detection_run_id bigint [not null, ref: > detection_runs.id]
  license_plan_id bigint [not null, ref: > license_plans.id]
  org_unit_id bigint [ref: > org_units.id, note: 'Unit the result belongs to (D10). NULL only for inactive or leaver seats of holders with Unknown unit']
  check_type detection_check [not null]
  flagged_qty numeric(20,4) [note: 'Unassigned seats, inactive seats, or seats allocated above purchased. NULL = not evaluated; 0 = clear; more than 0 = flagged']
  monthly_cost numeric(18,2) [note: 'Monthly cost of the flagged quantity, in the reporting currency; NULL = Unknown']
  flagged_since date [note: 'First day of the current unbroken flagged streak']
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (detection_run_id, license_plan_id, check_type, org_unit_id) [unique, name: 'uq_detection_results_run_plan_check_unit']
    check_type
    license_plan_id
    org_unit_id
  }

  checks {
    `check_type in ('inactive', 'leaver') or org_unit_id is not null` [name: 'chk_detection_results_unit']
    `flagged_qty is null or flagged_qty >= 0` [name: 'chk_detection_results_flagged_qty']
    `(coalesce(flagged_qty, 0) > 0) = (flagged_since is not null)` [name: 'chk_detection_results_since']
  }

  Note: '''
    Result of one check for one license and unit in one run: only the
    verdict is stored (flagged quantity, its monthly cost, since when). Not
    evaluated, clear, and flagged are read from flagged_qty: NULL, 0, more
    than 0. A result shows its evidence, its cost, and the data date (BR-12).
    Unit of a result (D10):
      unused   one row for the owner unit of the license (unassigned seats sit
               in Unallocated of the owner, BR-06)
      overuse  one row for the owner unit
      inactive one row per unit of the holders; NULL = Unknown unit
      leaver   same as inactive (D20)
    Leaver check (D20): open seats whose subject is disabled at the provider
    (is_enabled = false) or whose employee has a left_on before the data date.
    A seat flagged as leaver is not counted again in inactive.
    Shared and service accounts (BR-28) are judged as whole accounts and
    listed apart in UC11, never as an inactive person.
    Manager data scope (BR-16): a Manager sees the rows of their units, plus the
    Unknown-unit rows of the licenses their units own.
    Lists and dashboards read the same rows, so figures tie across screens
    (UC10, UC11, UC18). Not evaluated (flagged_qty NULL) when the coverage of
    the data date is not complete (D8) or the figures needed are Unknown.
    The figures shown beside a result are read from their owner table for the
    data date of the run, never copied here:
      Purchased               = plan_daily_snapshots.purchased_qty
      Assigned, seat statuses = plan_unit_daily_snapshots
      Peak, deployed units    = usage_records
      Unassigned, Excess      = flagged_qty
    The per-seat list of UC11 is the current list of license_assignments: it
    is shown for the latest run only; older runs keep their counts, not names.
    The unique index needs NULLS NOT DISTINCT because org_unit_id may be NULL.
  '''
}

Table recommendations {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  license_plan_id bigint [not null, ref: > license_plans.id]
  target_plan_id bigint [ref: > license_plans.id, note: 'For downgrade_plan: the plan to move to, of the same product']
  org_unit_id bigint [ref: > org_units.id, note: 'Unit the recommendation concerns, for Manager data scope (D10); NULL = holders with Unknown department']
  detection_result_id bigint [ref: > detection_results.id, note: 'Result it was created from; NULL when created by hand']
  type recommendation_type [not null]
  title varchar(300) [not null]
  description text
  evidence jsonb [not null, note: 'Snapshot of the evidence at creation time (BR-13)']
  affected_qty numeric(20,4)
  estimated_yearly_saving numeric(18,2) [note: 'In the reporting currency. NULL = Unknown, when the price is not known (D15)']
  actual_saving numeric(18,2) [note: 'Entered in the reporting currency when marked done']
  status recommendation_status [not null, default: 'proposed']
  rejection_reason text
  contract_id bigint [ref: > contracts.id, note: 'Contract whose renewal limits when this can be acted on (UC13). NULL = can be acted on at any time (monthly, pay-as-you-go)']
  due_date date [note: 'Internal deadline set for the owner; not the notice deadline of the contract']
  owner_id bigint [ref: > user_accounts.id]
  created_by bigint [not null, ref: > user_accounts.id]
  decided_by bigint [ref: > user_accounts.id]
  decided_at timestamptz
  done_at timestamptz
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (license_plan_id, type)
    status
    org_unit_id
    owner_id
    contract_id
  }

  checks {
    `status <> 'rejected' or rejection_reason is not null` [name: 'chk_recommendations_reject_reason']
    `status <> 'done' or (done_at is not null and actual_saving is not null)` [name: 'chk_recommendations_done']
    `(status in ('accepted', 'rejected', 'done')) = (decided_at is not null)` [name: 'chk_recommendations_decided']
    `estimated_yearly_saving is null or estimated_yearly_saving >= 0` [name: 'chk_recommendations_saving']
    `(type = 'downgrade_plan') = (target_plan_id is not null)` [name: 'chk_recommendations_target_plan']
    `target_plan_id is null or target_plan_id <> license_plan_id` [name: 'chk_recommendations_target_differs']
  }

  Note: '''
    Retired (D38): UC13 and UC14 are retired and ELMS does not track actions on
    licenses. The table is kept and not written.
    Former use: recommendations and their decision (UC14, BR-13):
    proposed -> accepted or rejected (reason required) -> done (actual saving
    required). ELMS never carries one out on the provider (BR-01).
    An Unknown estimated saving is shown as Unknown and left out of saving
    totals, which count it separately (D15).
    Notice deadline (UC13, D16) is computed on read from the contract:
    renewal_date - notice_period_days, Unknown when either is NULL. It is not
    copied here, so a corrected renewal date or notice period is seen at once.
    Partial unique: one open recommendation per plan, type, and unit
    (unique on license_plan_id, type, org_unit_id where status in
    (proposed, accepted), with NULLS NOT DISTINCT).
    App rule: only an accepted recommendation can be marked done; the target
    plan belongs to the same product; the contract covers a line of the plan.
  '''
}

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 7. Audit (BR-14, BR-15)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

Table audit_logs {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  actor_id bigint [ref: > user_accounts.id, note: 'NULL for system jobs']
  action varchar(50) [not null, note: 'create, update, deactivate, activate, status_change, role_change, permission_change, import ...']
  entity_type varchar(60) [not null, note: 'Table name of the changed row']
  entity_id bigint [not null, note: 'id of the changed row; every table has a single-column id']
  old_values jsonb
  new_values jsonb
  reason text [note: 'Required where a rule asks for one: permission change (UC22), unit correction (UC20)']
  correlation_id varchar(64) [note: 'Request id, or sync_run / job id for system changes']
  ip_address varchar(45)
  occurred_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (entity_type, entity_id, occurred_at)
    (actor_id, occurred_at)
    occurred_at
  }

  Note: '''
    Append-only record of who changed what, with old value, new value, and time
    (BR-15): connectors (create, edit, pause, resume), budget imports,
    catalog mappings, shared-license marks, expenses, users, units, roles,
    and permissions. The application database role has INSERT
    and SELECT only on this table, so rows cannot be updated or deleted.
  '''
}

Table data_overrides {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  entity_type varchar(60) [not null, note: 'Table name: org_units (UC20)']
  entity_id bigint [not null]
  field_name varchar(60) [not null]
  original_value text [note: 'Value from the connector; refreshed by each sync']
  override_value text [not null]
  reason text [not null]
  overridden_by bigint [not null, ref: > user_accounts.id]
  overridden_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  reverted_at timestamptz [note: 'NULL = the override is in force']

  indexes {
    (entity_type, entity_id, field_name)
  }

  Note: '''
    Admin correction of a value that came from ILVG (UC20): a unit placed
    under the wrong parent, with a reason; the original value is kept beside
    it. While an override is in force, an ILVG sync updates original_value here
    and leaves the corrected column. Licenses, holders, and usage are never
    overridden: they are corrected at the source (BR-01).
    Values are text in one format: numbers as plain decimals, dates as ISO 8601.
    Partial unique: one override in force per field
    (unique on entity_type, entity_id, field_name where reverted_at is null).
    App rule: the sync and an Admin edit lock the edited row (SELECT ... FOR
    UPDATE) so neither overwrites the other.
  '''
}

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Table groups
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

TableGroup organization_and_access {
  org_units
  employees
  roles
  permissions
  role_permissions
  user_accounts
